# Keep the build context to what the image is built FROM.
#
# Without this the context carries app/build/ (a previous web bundle, tens of
# megabytes), every .dart_tool/ and every coverage/ directory — all of it
# uploaded to the daemon on each build, and app/build/ in particular would be
# COPYed over the one this image is about to compile.

**/.dart_tool/
**/build/
**/coverage/
**/.flutter-plugins-dependencies

# One environment's public web config, for a developer's `flutter build web`.
# The image takes its configuration from build args instead (Dockerfile,
# Decision 1), so a file left over from somebody's Hosting build must not
# reach the context and must never be mistaken for the image's input.
app/config/firebase.json

.git/
